---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import {url, github} from '../../lib/content';
---
<Page title="Quickstart">
  <article class="docs-layout quickstart">
    <a class="backlink" href={url('docs/')}>← Docs</a>
    <h1>Quickstart</h1>
    <p id="local">Download a build from <a href={url('#install')}>Install Animatix</a> and extract it. Save <a href={url('content/scenes/insertion-sort.amx')} download>insertion-sort.amx</a> to that folder, or <a href={url('playground/?scene=insertion-sort&step=four')}>edit it in your browser</a>.</p>
    <section id="gui" aria-labelledby="gui-title">
      <h2 id="gui-title">GUI</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Launch <code>animatix-gui</code>. Open the <code>.amx</code> file from the filename menu.</li>
        <li>Choose <strong>Write</strong> to change the source. Change the <code>1.25s</code> on the <code>four.at</code> line to <code>1.6s</code> to slow the move.</li>
        <li>Choose <strong>Review</strong> and scrub to <code>7.6s</code> to see the move in progress. Save the file when you’re done.</li>
      </ol>
      <a class="text-link" href={github + '/blob/main/docs/gui-workbench.md'}>Workbench guide ↗</a>
    </section>
    <section id="cli" aria-labelledby="cli-title">
      <h2 id="cli-title">CLI</h2>
      <p>From the extracted folder, validate the scene and render a still.</p>
      <pre><code>{`./bin/animatix check insertion-sort.amx
./bin/animatix image insertion-sort.amx --time 7.6 --output frame.png`}</code></pre>
      <p>Use a video-enabled build to render the full scene to MP4.</p>
      <pre><code>./bin/animatix video insertion-sort.amx --output insertion-sort.mp4</code></pre>
      <p class="quickstart-note">On macOS, use <code>./animatix</code>. On Windows, use <code>{String.raw`.\animatix.exe`}</code>.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Page>
